# How the cheatsheet's reference half is grouped into categories.
#
# The DIGEST -- the first screen -- is not configured here. It comes from the
# three `###` blocks of the "Every Day" section of docs/keybindings.md, one per
# column. Everything else is reference, and this file says which category each
# group of binds lands in.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. DMS ignores the order categories appear in the JSON.
# Modals/KeybindsContent.qml sorts them by estimated height, descending, then
# greedy-packs each into the shortest column:
#
#     const sorted = [...categoryKeys].sort(
#         (a, b) => estimateCategoryHeight(b) - estimateCategoryHeight(a));
#
# With three empty columns the three TALLEST categories therefore land at the
# top of the three columns. That is the only lever over what sits above the
# fold, so the digest wins it by being taller than every category below --
# which means every category here must stay under the cap. The generator
# asserts exactly that, so a group that grows too large fails the build instead
# of silently displacing the digest.
#
# Format: source group|category it belongs to
# A source group is a `###` heading from docs/keybindings.md or a
# `// -- Section --` heading from the niri binds.kdl. Every group must appear
# here exactly once, and every line must name a group that exists.

